  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Token + Position Embedding** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(token_ids, token_embeddings, position_embeddings):\n    ids=np.asarray(token_ids,dtype=int); te=np.asarray(token_embeddings,dtype=float); pe=np.asarray(position_embeddings,dtype=float)\n    if len(ids)>len(pe): raise ValueError(\"not enough position embeddings\")\n    return (te[ids]+pe[:len(ids)]).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
